Z||000009||fiero56||12-14-1999||11:59 PM||||Works for me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. So, you have two regular Fieros and one parts car. Where do you guys find these parts cars? I don't need one, but I never see them around, and there are no "recycling" centers anywhere near my house.||||reg||7
Z||000010||Cooter||12-15-1999||12:45 AM||||No, I have the two complete red cars and 3 additional parts cars. The 86 GT, a very wrecked 85 coupe and a complete 85 coupe. I have a retired friend that keeps buying these things up. He sees them in people's back yards and offers to haul them away of give a couple of hundred bucks for them. Around here, there are numerous junk yards and no laws against having junk cars in your yard, so you can find them if you go out looking.||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||12-15-1999||08:55 AM||||I forgot about that law. We have a law here, "non-running vehicles must be in garage or under a tarp, but not touching your lawn." Must be why I never see junk cars around. I don't think dayton/centerville has a junk yard, nobody knows of one around here. Closest one would probably be Cinci.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-15-1999||04:17 PM||||fiero56--If you ever get to Middletown, try some of thiers.  I just bought 2 complete doors from an '86 SE with all the working options incl ground effects for $150.  They had some other stuff, too, but I ran out of money.  I'll get their name if you're interested.  I have their card somewhere.  Indiana has the same sort of law, except they don't care as long as they're not visible from the street or have a current plate.  I've seen some pretty crappy cars around here with current plates (obviously parts cars).||||reg||1
Z||000013||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||05:50 PM||||fiero56,<P>Boy you must only stay in the Centerville area of Dayton.  Dayton has MANY more j-yards than Cinci (at least within a close proximity).  I know of several large yards that often have many cars in the Dayton Area.  Both are N. & E. of you though.  I need to go to the yards before it gets too cold.  Otherwise, you can come down to Middletucky (my home town) as Monkey suggested.  Arts Parts and Service always has at least 3 Fiero's.  Let me know... call me at work 937-259-5295 (I am there most of the time...8-????)<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000014||Monkeyman||12-16-1999||01:20 AM||||Arts was the place I got the doors from.  They seem to be fairly easy to work with.  The other ones on Oxford State Rd. suck, though, unless I missed one.||||reg||1
